### 2. Infrastructure Hardening (Stopping AWS Theft)

The absolute safest and most un-hackable way to stop Docker containers from stealing IAM roles inside AWS is to drop packets natively at the host's iptables engine or via AWS Hop limits.

#### [NEW] [ec2-hardening.sh](file:///c:/Users/het70/Desktop/latesteditor/backend/scripts/ec2-hardening.sh)
-   Write a deployment bash script that you can run once on your host EC2 instance.
-   It will inject a permanent `iptables` rule dropping all traffic originating from the Docker interface bounds destined for the infamous AWS Metadata IP (`169.254.169.254`).
-   It will include quick instructions on locking EC2 down via IMDSv2 Hop Limits (the secondary best-practice for AWS).

